# Files the STORE owns, not the repo.
#
# `shopify theme push` overwrites the store from local files, so anything here
# holding merchant configuration would undo theme-editor work on every push.

# Global theme settings: colour schemes, typography, favicon, social links.
# Never edited from the repo, so it is ignored in both directions.
config/settings_data.json

# NOTE: templates/index.json is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It holds the page's sections and their settings, so pushing it blindly does
# revert editor work — but .shopifyignore applies to pull and dev as well, and
# ignoring it would also block `theme dev` from syncing editor changes back
# down, which is how configuration reaches the repo in the first place.
#
# Handled by sequence instead of by exclusion:
#
#   shopify theme pull --theme "Assignment" --only templates/index.json
#   git add templates/index.json && git commit -m "chore: sync page config"
#   shopify theme push --theme "Assignment"
#
# Pull down, commit, then push. `theme dev` does the first step continuously
# while it is running.
